From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:18:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hnetcfg: authorized applications and open ports over the
 stored rules

INetFwAuthorizedApplications and INetFwOpenPorts, the older interfaces installers still use,
count, find, enumerate and remove what they added: a program allowed is an inbound allow rule
for its path without ports, a port opened one for a single TCP or UDP port without a program.
The program and port objects keep and pass on IP version, scope and remote addresses
(Scope and RemoteAddresses agree: all is "*", local subnet "LocalSubnet", else custom), Enabled
and BuiltIn work, and Item of something not there fails with ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND. Removing needs
an administrator (the registry refuses anyone else) and is told to Stained Glass Firewall at once.

diff --git a/dlls/hnetcfg/apps.c b/dlls/hnetcfg/apps.c
